!Sample_last_update_date = Sep 30 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = prostate
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Prostate cancer cell line LNCaP
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = procedure: Chromatin IP against AR
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = chip antibody: AR (sc-816; Santa Cruz)
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Cells were treated with 10nM R1881 or vehicle for 4 hours.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = LNCaP cells were cultured in RPMI-1640 supplemented with 10% FBS. Cells were hormone deprived three days before R1881 stimulation.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Chromatin immunoprecipitations (ChIP) were performed as described (Stelloo et al. Embo Mol Med 2015) For each ChIP, 5-10μg of antibody prebound to protein A or protein G beads was used.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were prepared according to Illumina's instructions accompanying the DNA Sample Kit (Kapa Biosystems kit,KK8234).
!Sample_data_processing = Sequences were generated by the Illumina Hiseq 2500 genome analyser (using 65bp reads) and were processed by the Illumina pipeline.
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned to the Human Reference Genome (hg19) using BWA version 0.5.9. Reads with a BWA alignment quality score less than 20 were removed.
!Sample_data_processing = Peaks were called using DFilter (Kumar V et al. Nat Biotechnol 2013;31(7):615-22) and MACS peak caller version 1.4 (Zhang Y et al. Genome Biol 2008;9(9):R137). Only peaks called by both algorithms were used for the analysis. MACS was run with the default parameters, except p=10-5. DFilter was run with bs=50, ks=30, refine, nonzero.
